Z||000000||mrfixit58||03-04-2000||10:55 AM||||I wrote one of the guys who are racing the 4900 Caddy V8 Fiero. Below is his update on their progress:<P>"Check out our web site @ <A HREF="http://www.azstarnet.com/~gduncan" TARGET=_blank>http://www.azstarnet.com/~gduncan</A> <BR>We have been 'tuning' the system since about April. Some days are better<BR>than others if you know what I mean. As far as the engine goes....it's a<BR>hoot to drive. I would heartily recommend installing an MSD ignition<BR>along with ACCEL plugs and SuperCoil. Those tied in with some<BR>performance oriented plug wires wake the engine up dramatically. We are<BR>running a true dual exhaust through 2 1/2" pipes with Walker bullet<BR>mufflers. At PIR we can hold off the 'Vettes and other V-8 cars on the<BR>straights. When we came onto the oval from the 'hairpin', we were<BR>tailing a Viper. He only had two car lengths on us by the time we hit<BR>turn #1. Our plans for the future are to convert to 1.7:1 full roller<BR>rockers and get rid of the factory rev limiter.<P>Later,<BR>Tom"<P>I keep wondering how the cost of this conversion compairs with the Northstar.<P>Roy L.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||olympic||03-04-2000||03:51 PM||||I'll bet you can buy this engine out of a wrecked caddy for about 1/4 the price(or less) of a Northstar. I've heard that the trannys that came with these engines were not the greatest though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||03-04-2000||09:25 PM||||I thought his web site said they bolted the 4900 to a Fiero tranny. I know they are running a Getrag 5-speed. Seems like one of there major cost was in making the special flywheel and the kevlar clutch. The swap would be even cheaper with a th125. Neet idea.<P>Roy L.||||reg||5
